{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":47995,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a9e8edb7-509d-543c-a103-d57cfa800193","total_cost_usd":0.39966799999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8611,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4455,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8611,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4455,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8611,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8611},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4568,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004678,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4455,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":8611,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.39498999999999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:dependence-free-batch-b-reviewer-fable-18\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:bf08b2218ca9cef1db2d\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The data description names basin_id as the independent-unit column and states every basin code appears exactly once, with one survey visit per basin.\", \"observed_value\": \"one row per basin_id; no repeat visits\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 10, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"One row is: one drained peat basin, surveyed a single time, with its ditch treatment and its yes/no Sphagnum re-establishment outcome\\n\\nIndependent unit column: basin_id\"}, {\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 16, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"- basin_id: the survey code for the basin. Every code appears exactly once, so\\n  the file has as many rows as there are basins.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Direct inspection of data/input.csv shows 24 data rows with 24 distinct basin_id values (PB-01 through PB-24), each occurring exactly once; no independent unit contributes more than one row to the analysis.\", \"observed_value\": \"24 rows, 24 unique basin_id values, 0 duplicates\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 2, \"quoted_text\": \"basin_id,catchment,ditch_treatment,basin_area_ha,peat_depth_cm,sphagnum_reestablished\\nPB-01,Lang Fell,blocked,12.4,210,yes\"}, {\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 25, \"end_line\": 25, \"quoted_text\": \"PB-24,Corrie Burn,open,6.7,225,no\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow actively enforces uniqueness of the independent unit before analysis: load_basins raises a ValueError if any basin_id occurs more than once, so a repeated-unit entry could not silently reach the row-independent Fisher test.\", \"observed_value\": \"duplicate guard on basin_id in load_basins\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 25, \"end_line\": 30, \"quoted_text\": \"    seen = set()\\n    for row in rows:\\n        unit = row[UNIT_COLUMN]\\n        if unit in seen:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"basin recorded more than once: \\\" + unit)\\n        seen.add(unit)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The reported contingency table matches an independent hand tally of the CSV at one row per basin: blocked basins yield 9 yes / 3 no (PB-01, 03, 05, 09, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23 yes; PB-07, 15, 21 no) and open basins yield 3 yes / 9 no (PB-04, 12, 20 yes), so no unit's outcome is counted more than once in the test input.\", \"observed_value\": \"[[9, 3], [3, 9]] confirmed from unique rows; arms of 12 and 12 sum to 24\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"| blocked | 12 | 9 | 0.750 | 14.58 | 207.5 |\\n| open | 12 | 3 | 0.250 | 14.25 | 207.5 |\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"Contingency table (rows: blocked, open; columns: yes, no): [[9, 3], [3, 9]]\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"2025 growing season. Basins are the independent units: 24 basins, 24 rows,\\nand no basin appears twice.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The only feature that could be mistaken for repeated-unit entry is the catchment column: the 24 basins are grouped into three named catchments (Lang Fell, Tarn Moss, Corrie Burn), which could raise a separate spatial-clustering concern. However, catchment is not the stated independent unit (basin_id is), the description marks catchment as descriptive only, and no catchment-level unit is entered repeatedly as if it were the independent unit; this is therefore not an instance of the reviewed issue class.\", \"observed_value\": \"3 catchments x 8 basins each; catchment declared descriptive only\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 12, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"Independent unit column: basin_id\"}, {\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 3, \"quoted_text\": \"PB-02,Lang Fell,open,16.2,165,no\\nPB-03,Lang Fell,blocked,8.7,145,yes\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching for any independent unit contributing multiple rows to the row-independent Fisher's exact test. I scanned all 24 data rows of data/input.csv for duplicate basin_id values and found none (PB-01 through PB-24 each appear exactly once). I checked whether the workflow could aggregate or re-enter units multiple times: summarise() partitions rows by ditch_treatment and counts each row once, and load_basins() would raise an error on any duplicate basin_id, so duplicates cannot pass silently. I re-derived the contingency table by hand from the CSV and reproduced [[9, 3], [3, 9]] with arm sizes 12 and 12 summing to the 24 unique basins, matching the report's claim of 24 independent basins. I also considered whether a coarser unit (catchment) was being repeatedly entered as though independent, but basin_id is the declared independent unit and each basin was surveyed once, so no repeated-entry construction exists. Every attempt to find repeated independent-unit entry failed.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":26013,"ttft_stream_ms":1657,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":48663,"uuid":"08982b97-5b8e-4ec4-a6f9-f91a80f3188c"}
